{"fn_name": "opng_strparse_rangeset_to_bitset", "rule_id": "III④,II_vec,III③,C3", "round_no": 1, "attempt_no": 1, "status": "applied_committed", "w1_result": "pass", "w2_delta_pct": -25.741566678852458, "commit_sha": "355a414", "tokens_in": 38993, "tokens_out": 3492, "error": null, "reason": null, "fired_rules": ["C3", "C4", "III③", "III④", "II_vec"], "applied_rules": ["C3"], "skipped_rules": [["C4", "The loop is a parser over a NUL-terminated C string with per-byte state-machine work, digit accumulation, delimiter handling, and whitespace classification; it is not a pure byte-scan/equality cursor loop, so word-at-a-time widening would not match the rule's safety/perf envelope. No concrete C4 hit will be addressed."], ["III③", "__errno_location hits [14, 15] are not manual memory/string operations in scope for this rule; replacing them would be semantic/API churn rather than the intended mem/string rewrite."], ["C3", "Signature-lift S1 is abstained because this function is #[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" and changing pointer parameters to references/slices would break the C ABI."], ["III④", "no_fingerprint(F9 stripped)"], ["II_vec", "no_fingerprint(F9 stripped)"]], "plan_json": {"applied_rules": [{"rule": "III④", "strategy": "Reborrow the input C string as a byte slice/CStr inside the body and replace repeated raw-pointer post-increment cursor walks with indexed/iterator-style traversal over bytes while preserving the extern ABI.", "target_hits": [16, 17, 18, 19, 20], "needs_cross_fn": false, "rationale": "This is the primary structural rewrite: the function is pub extern \"C\", so signature lift is off-limits, but an in-body view can still recover length information from the NUL terminator (L4) and eliminate most raw cursor churn. Doing III④ first subsumes much of the C3 aliasing-gap symptom and addresses the same loop shape that II_vec complained about. It also makes the isspace-driven whitespace skips candidates for typed byte predicates instead of opaque libcalls."}, {"rule": "II_vec", "strategy": "Canonicalize the parser loop away from the current_block state-machine shape into structured control flow over a byte iterator/index so LLVM can see iteration structure and remove vectorization blockers where profitable.", "target_hits": [7, 8, 9, 10, 11], "needs_cross_fn": false, "rationale": "The loop currently mixes a goto-emulation state machine with sentinel-driven cursor advancement and opaque calls, which directly matches the reported CantComputeNumberOfIterations/CantVectorizeLibcall failures. Applying this after III④ is important because the slice/CStr view gives a cleaner traversal substrate; then the control-flow cleanup can be localized and may also make several C3 load remarks disappear as a byproduct."}, {"rule": "III③", "strategy": "Replace the opaque character-classification/libc-style calls used in the hot traversal with typed Rust/CStr equivalents where semantics are straightforward, while leaving errno writeback handling alone.", "target_hits": [12, 13], "needs_cross_fn": false, "rationale": "The two isspace sites are inside the traversal and are exactly the libcall barriers reported by II_vec. Converting them after III④/II_vec lets the rewrite use byte-based predicates on the already-established view instead of raw-pointer calls. __errno_location is not a memory-op/string-op replacement candidate here and should not be forced into III③."}, {"rule": "C3", "strategy": "Use local caching / single-byte local variables for repeatedly-read current characters and loop-invariant view state once the traversal is expressed over a local slice/index, avoiding redundant reloads from the raw pointer path.", "target_hits": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], "needs_cross_fn": false, "rationale": "Because the ABI must remain raw, C3.S1 is unavailable; only S2-style local hoisting/caching is viable. This should be done last because the larger III④ + II_vec + III③ structural cleanup may already eliminate many repeated loads, and any remaining hot reloads can then be targeted precisely without adding noise."}], "abstained_rules": [{"rule": "C4", "reason": "The loop is a parser over a NUL-terminated C string with per-byte state-machine work, digit accumulation, delimiter handling, and whitespace classification; it is not a pure byte-scan/equality cursor loop, so word-at-a-time widening would not match the rule's safety/perf envelope. No concrete C4 hit will be addressed."}, {"rule": "III③", "reason": "__errno_location hits [14, 15] are not manual memory/string operations in scope for this rule; replacing them would be semantic/API churn rather than the intended mem/string rewrite."}, {"rule": "C3", "reason": "Signature-lift S1 is abstained because this function is #[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" and changing pointer parameters to references/slices would break the C ABI."}], "rewrite_order": ["III④", "II_vec", "III③", "C3"], "interactions_noted": ["Applying III④ to the ptr cursor sites provides a local byte-slice/CStr view that makes the II_vec loop canonicalization much simpler and may eliminate several raw-pointer reloads before C3 is attempted.", "III④ + II_vec together likely subsume most of the C3 gvn-load-clobbered hits by removing repeated dereferences of *ptr in the state machine.", "III③ on isspace directly addresses the II_vec CantVectorizeLibcall blockers at the whitespace-skip loops; doing it after III④ lets the replacement operate on bytes rather than raw c_char loads.", "C4 is intentionally not combined with III④ here: slice-ifying a parser loop is useful, but widening it to u64-at-a-time would not preserve the parser's branchy semantics or likely help performance.", "No cross-function rewrite is planned because the extern C ABI forbids signature changes; all improvements are body-local."], "risk_flags": ["Whitespace semantics risk: replacing isspace must preserve C-locale behavior for the byte domain actually accepted by this parser.", "Sentinel-derived view risk: any CStr/from_ptr or equivalent byte-slice construction relies on rangeset_str being non-null and NUL-terminated per caller contract.", "Control-flow rewrite risk: the current state machine encodes subtle parse/error transitions (state 0/1/2, err_invalid vs err_range); restructuring must preserve exact errno/result behavior."]}, "original_plan_json": {"applied_rules": [{"rule": "III④", "strategy": "Reborrow the input C string as a byte slice/CStr inside the body and replace repeated raw-pointer post-increment cursor walks with indexed/iterator-style traversal over bytes while preserving the extern ABI.", "target_hits": [16, 17, 18, 19, 20], "needs_cross_fn": false, "rationale": "This is the primary structural rewrite: the function is pub extern \"C\", so signature lift is off-limits, but an in-body view can still recover length information from the NUL terminator (L4) and eliminate most raw cursor churn. Doing III④ first subsumes much of the C3 aliasing-gap symptom and addresses the same loop shape that II_vec complained about. It also makes the isspace-driven whitespace skips candidates for typed byte predicates instead of opaque libcalls."}, {"rule": "II_vec", "strategy": "Canonicalize the parser loop away from the current_block state-machine shape into structured control flow over a byte iterator/index so LLVM can see iteration structure and remove vectorization blockers where profitable.", "target_hits": [7, 8, 9, 10, 11], "needs_cross_fn": false, "rationale": "The loop currently mixes a goto-emulation state machine with sentinel-driven cursor advancement and opaque calls, which directly matches the reported CantComputeNumberOfIterations/CantVectorizeLibcall failures. Applying this after III④ is important because the slice/CStr view gives a cleaner traversal substrate; then the control-flow cleanup can be localized and may also make several C3 load remarks disappear as a byproduct."}, {"rule": "III③", "strategy": "Replace the opaque character-classification/libc-style calls used in the hot traversal with typed Rust/CStr equivalents where semantics are straightforward, while leaving errno writeback handling alone.", "target_hits": [12, 13], "needs_cross_fn": false, "rationale": "The two isspace sites are inside the traversal and are exactly the libcall barriers reported by II_vec. Converting them after III④/II_vec lets the rewrite use byte-based predicates on the already-established view instead of raw-pointer calls. __errno_location is not a memory-op/string-op replacement candidate here and should not be forced into III③."}, {"rule": "C3", "strategy": "Use local caching / single-byte local variables for repeatedly-read current characters and loop-invariant view state once the traversal is expressed over a local slice/index, avoiding redundant reloads from the raw pointer path.", "target_hits": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], "needs_cross_fn": false, "rationale": "Because the ABI must remain raw, C3.S1 is unavailable; only S2-style local hoisting/caching is viable. This should be done last because the larger III④ + II_vec + III③ structural cleanup may already eliminate many repeated loads, and any remaining hot reloads can then be targeted precisely without adding noise."}], "abstained_rules": [{"rule": "C4", "reason": "The loop is a parser over a NUL-terminated C string with per-byte state-machine work, digit accumulation, delimiter handling, and whitespace classification; it is not a pure byte-scan/equality cursor loop, so word-at-a-time widening would not match the rule's safety/perf envelope. No concrete C4 hit will be addressed."}, {"rule": "III③", "reason": "__errno_location hits [14, 15] are not manual memory/string operations in scope for this rule; replacing them would be semantic/API churn rather than the intended mem/string rewrite."}, {"rule": "C3", "reason": "Signature-lift S1 is abstained because this function is #[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" and changing pointer parameters to references/slices would break the C ABI."}], "re